Not much of interest in this ascension except that I used darts a lot,
especially on Astral. Of note, the Wizard stole my uberweapon, the
Staff of Aesculapius, twice, and I was forced to defeat him with
blessed rustproof +7 darts. It didn't take very long, because darts
rock at +7 expert and they never missed.

Yeah, a lot of stuff went wrong on the ascension run. First, I
discovered that uncursed scrolls of teleportation aren't a reliable
levelport method when read stunned + confused the hard way: after
killing Rodney, I attempted to levelport to the VS but instead was
sent all the way to level 1 and had to dig / climb down to the VoTD
for another levelport.

Second, I quaffed all the non-dilute potions of full healing for HP
and relied on the diluted ones for healing. When I dropped by the
Wizard's moat for a swim, I discovered my seven diluted potions of
full healing were now seven potions of water damnit. I only had two
potions of full healing for the entire ascension run.

Third, I discovered the utility of the Repair Armor spell, which saved
my gauntlets and CoMR from certain doom many times. Unfortunately, I
neglected my +5 boots of speed, which disintegrated early in the run.
Thankfully, I also respect the utility of polypiling and had two
spares. ;)

Fourth, *do not polypile wands of digging for any reason* AAGH I
almost got stuck at Asmodeus and had to tame an Umber hulk to chew a
route *away* from the horde of summoned nasties on the level.

On Astral, I had life saving, but was scared to death due to my lack
of healing potions. I resolved to cut down the Kill the Newly Arrived
Adventurer Club one angel and player monster at a time from afar.
Famine, four priests, and two player monsters bit the dust to poisoned
darts, clearing a path to the first (thankfully neutral!) high altar.
Damn, good luck for me. In retrospect, I wish I had level-drained and
tamed Pesty and Famine so I'd have something unusual to brag about,
but nope, except "I ascended", which is worth bragging about
regardless.

Corwin, neutral male human Healer






